From 9046e49f252c6ce79fb73a2ce396be7cbd41a2f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jared Massie <you@example.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 01:44:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add a stable release-signing keystore so future updates
 install in place
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every previous build was signed with a throwaway debug key CI generated
fresh each run, so each new APK's signature differed from whatever was
already installed and Android refused to update ("package conflicts with
an existing package"). This adds a committed keystore + key.properties and
wires the release build type to sign with it consistently — one more
uninstall/reinstall is needed to get onto this key, but every build after
this one will update in place.
---
 android/app/blockit-release.keystore | Bin 0 -> 2730 bytes
 android/app/build.gradle             |  37 ++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 android/key.properties               |   4 +++
 3 files changed, 38 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 android/app/blockit-release.keystore
 create mode 100644 android/key.properties

